74b2117ff0c7eb6fd71943c4ca021c6a364ab9e7","position":"1786061961471362001-f7eb4671-f805-487f-976f-4725d79d5ec9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"a4c9df7808bb68445ae748709c71311b3b2268a30b0994c5302a0c8d8f62bd45","event_uuid":"81881a86-6f9c-4936-8147-4c5c343637cf","position":{"commit_sha":"74b2117ff0c7eb6fd71943c4ca021c6a364ab9e7","position":"1786061962012139001-81881a86-6f9c-4936-8147-4c5c343637cf"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan-review pass 1 (frontier, live Bedrock) returned unsigned BLOCK with 2 findings (run also hit an LLM retry-exhaustion after emitting the verdict): G6 — the non-memoization predicate keyed on RAISED exceptions, but the allowlisted read-only tools (pai_tools.py) never raise; they return 'Error: …' strings for failures and deterministic '(no matches)'/'(empty)'/'(empty range)' sentinels for honest-empty. T8 — the FULL/skeleton manifest 'already-in-context' branch (and its AC) depends on the pre-loading sibling's manifest, whose shape/accessor is undefined and ships AFTER this ticket. Revised plan: (G6) redefined the predicate — errors = 'Error:'-prefixed strings (not memoized, not nudged, re-execute on retry); deterministic sentinel-empty like '(no matches)' IS memoized (the core 62x-loop waste case). (T8) deferred all manifest/in-context coupling to the pre-loading ticket; this change adds none — every read_file executes on first sight, duplicates get memo + generic nudge only. AC updated accordingly (split error vs sentinel-empty; live capture now requires a durable docs/experiments/ artifact). Re-running review-plan clean.","timestamp":1786060781804910001}],"created_at":1786047351244680001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"8252757f-95ae-4c8a-8aa4-46d20b70e740","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"c827-2a23-cd00-473e"},{"link_uuid":"a75172cc-615e-4f59-aefb-1361f5b98731","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"8eb3-1f20-f395-4ea5"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nLive completion-gate captures show agentic runs wasting 40-70% of their request budget on DUPLICATE tool calls: one run repeated an identical search_files call 144x, another looped 62x on an honest \"(no matches)\" result. The shipped windowed distinct-ratio actuator (agent_call.py) correctly ABORTS pathological runs, but abortion is the backstop — nothing today prevents the waste before the trip point, and every duplicate re-executes the tool and re-pays the round-trip. Research across agent harnesses (OpenHands StuckDetector, smolagents max_steps) found detect-and-terminate everywhere but no harness that memoizes the duplicate and steers the model back on course — graduated nudge-then-abort is the recommended pattern.\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd a memoize+nudge toolset wrapper at the shared agent-call seam (src/rebar/llm/agent_call.py), the module that already arms every tool-bearing Agent call: wrapper order runaway guard OUTERMOST -> memo -> steering (guard :68, steering :45; the guard's call_tool observes the signature before the memo short-circuits, so the actuator's window math is unchanged).\n\n- Key: the EXISTING usage_log tool-call signature (identical normalization to the actuator — same signature means same dedup semantics).\n- Behavior: first repeat of a signature returns the cached result plus a static templated nudge line; further repeats return the cached result plus a stronger static nudge; the distinct-ratio actuator remains the abort backstop. Static text only — a templated nudge keeps message content byte-stable for provider prompt caching.\n- Non-memoization predicate (keyed on how the allowlisted tools ACTUALLY signal, pai_tools.py): these tools NEVER raise into the agent loop — they return strings. An ERROR result is one whose text begins with the \"Error:\" prefix (read_file/list_directory/search_files/show_ticket all return f\"Error: {exc}\" on ValueError/OSError). Error results are NOT memoized and NOT nudged: the identical call re-executes on retry, because a transient/again-different outcome is possible. By contrast the deterministic \"sentinel-empty\" results — \"(no matches)\" (search_files), \"(empty)\" (list_directory), \"(empty range)\" (read_file) — are HONEST, stable answers and ARE memoized+nudged: memoizing \"(no matches)\" is precisely the 62x-loop waste this ticket eliminates. (The \"UNRESOLVED\" resolve_symbol sentinel is moot here — resolve_symbol is not in the allowlist below.)\n- Read-only allowlist: only read_file, search_files, list_directory, and show_ticket are memoized (all four exist in the verifier toolset, pai_tools.py:243); write or non-deterministic tools — including the banked-verification sibling's record_criterion_verdict — are exempt.\n- No manifest / in-context awareness in THIS ticket: the FULL/skeleton \"already in context\" nudge depends on the pre-loading sibling's manifest, whose shape, marker vocabulary, and accessor are not yet defined and ship AFTER this change. This ticket therefore adds NO manifest coupling: every allowlisted read_file executes normally on first sight and returns the real content; duplicates get memoization plus the generic repeat nudge only. The manifest-aware FULL-branch nudge is deferred to the pre-loading ticket, which will layer it on this seam.\n\n## Scope\n\n- src/rebar/llm/agent_call.py — the memo wrapper + wrapper-order wiring (guard -> memo -> steering).\n- tests/unit/test_agent_call_memo_nudge.py — new: memo semantics, wrapper order, allowlist, error passthrough (Error:-prefixed strings re-execute), sentinel-empty memoization (\"(no matches)\" cached), nudge escalation.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A duplicate allowlisted call returns the cached result without re-executing the tool; the wrapped tool function runs exactly once for N identical calls (unit test with a counting stub).\n- [ ] Nudge escalation: first repeat carries the level-1 static nudge, subsequent repeats the level-2 text; both byte-stable across runs (unit test).\n- [ ] The runaway guard still observes memoized duplicates: the distinct-ratio window sees every duplicate signature, and a synthetic loop still trips the actuator at the same call index with the memo active (unit test against the existing guard tests' fixtures).\n- [ ] Error results are not memoized: an allowlisted call whose return begins with \"Error:\" re-executes on the next identical call (counting stub returning an \"Error:\"-prefixed string, then a success), and carries no nudge (unit test).\n- [ ] Deterministic sentinel-empty results ARE memoized: a search_files-style stub returning \"(no matches)\" runs exactly once for N identical calls and the duplicate carries the repeat nudge (unit test) — the core waste case.\n- [ ] Only allowlisted read-only tools are memoized; record_criterion_verdict and any non-allowlisted tool always execute (unit test).\n- [ ] Live Bedrock capture recorded on this ticket: a run demonstrating either a nudge-broken loop (duplicate signature followed by a different next call) or a nudge->actuator escalation, with usage-log figures, backed by a durable in-repo artifact under docs/experiments/.\n- [ ] make lint and make typecheck pass; the existing runaway-guard unit suite (tests/unit/test_agent_call_runaway_guard_c827.py) passes unchanged.\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit suite in tests/unit/test_agent_call_memo_nudge.py per the acceptance criteria (counting stubs, wrapper-order assertion, guard-interaction fixture reuse, Error:-prefix passthrough, \"(no matches)\" memoization). Run: python -m pytest tests/unit/test_agent_call_memo_nudge.py tests/unit/test_agent_call_runaway_guard_c827.py -q. Live Bedrock capture per the live AC recorded as a durable artifact under docs/experiments/ plus a ticket comment. make lint + make typecheck.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/agent_call.py","reason":"memo wrapper + guard->memo->steering wiring"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_agent_call_memo_nudge.py","reason":"new: memo semantics, wrapper order, allowlist, error passthrough, nudge escalation, manifest gating"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["depends_on","8eb3-1f20-f395-4ea5"],["parent","10ae-aa24-3fdc-4f0b"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"10ae-aa24-3fdc-4f0b","parent_status_uuid":"f7eb4671-f805-487f-976f-4725d79d5ec9","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"f6fc-27fe-d3af-4f87","ticket_type":"story","title":"Memoize and nudge duplicate read-only tool calls at the shared agent-call seam","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["c02f3a67-eeca-4048-843d-c24429bd8ac7","6689308d-dd3d-4017-9da7-b06adbad1a30","8252757f-95ae-4c8a-8aa4-46d20b70e740","a75172cc-615e-4f59-aefb-1361f5b98731","38a72e50-148f-463f-8a3a-03a183b417b3","4bf05e9e-bb5d-44a3-b3f9-4c962bb2920a","8c29853a-de20-4c69-aa6a-b501094c777d","f7eb4671-f805-487f-976f-4725d79d5ec9","81881a86-6f9c-4936-8147-4c5c343637cf"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786061962012139002,"uuid":"092afb37-ad7f-443f-a425-6822f24536a2"}